            <ArticleTitle>[Case of palpebral nystagmus with a benign course].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of eye-lid nystagmus, synchronous to a vertical nystagmus, in a 35 year old female patient is extensively presented. Vestibular examinations and BAEPs were suggestive of an impairment of pontomesencephalic structures. Following an aspecific drug therapy the s. had a noticeable improvement with reduction of the symptomatology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
